# Photos & RGPD — Clean Connect

> Activé sur `apps/api/src/modules/photos/**`.
> Cahier des charges : §6.4 (sécurité) et §6.5 (RGPD).

---

## Upload — Signed URL Cloudinary

**Principe** : le mobile upload **directement** à Cloudinary, le backend ne transite jamais le binaire.

### Étape 1 — Le mobile demande une signature

```typescript
// POST /api/photos/sign
@Post('sign')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
async sign(@Body() dto: SignPhotoDto, @CurrentUser() user: AuthUser) {
  // dto : { uuid (client-generated), missionId, phase: 'BEFORE' | 'AFTER' }

  // Vérifier ownership : prestataire de cette mission ?
  await this.assertCanUploadPhoto(dto.missionId, user)

  // Idempotence : UUID déjà connu ?
  const existing = await this.prisma.photo.findUnique({ where: { uuid: dto.uuid } })
  if (existing) {
    return { idempotent: true, photoId: existing.id }
  }

  // Dossier privé par mission + phase
  const folder = `${env.NODE_ENV}/missions/${dto.missionId}/${dto.phase.toLowerCase()}`
  const publicId = `${folder}/${dto.uuid}`
  const timestamp = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)

  const signature = cloudinary.utils.api_sign_request(
    { public_id: publicId, timestamp, folder, type: 'private' },
    env.CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET,
  )

  // Pré-enregistrer la photo en DB avec status PENDING
  await this.prisma.photo.create({
    data: {
      uuid: dto.uuid,
      missionId: dto.missionId,
      phase: dto.phase,
      uploadedBy: user.id,
      cloudinaryPublicId: publicId,
      status: 'PENDING_UPLOAD',
    },
  })

  return { signature, timestamp, publicId, apiKey: env.CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, cloudName: env.CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME }
}
```

### Étape 2 — Le mobile upload à Cloudinary

(Côté mobile, voir `mobile.mdc`. Le serveur n'intervient pas dans le transit.)

### Étape 3 — Cloudinary notifie (webhook)

```typescript
@Post('cloudinary/webhook')
@HttpCode(HttpStatus.OK)
async cloudinaryWebhook(@Body() body: any, @Headers('x-cld-signature') sig: string) {
  if (!verifyCloudinarySignature(body, sig, env.CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET)) {
    throw new BadRequestException('Invalid signature')
  }

  if (body.notification_type === 'upload') {
    await this.prisma.photo.update({
      where: { cloudinaryPublicId: body.public_id },
      data: {
        status: 'UPLOADED',
        syncedAt: new Date(),
        width: body.width,
        height: body.height,
        bytes: body.bytes,
      },
    })
  }
}
```

